---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import content from '../data/content.json';
import {site} from '../data/site';
const story=content.find(page=>page.slug==='our-story')!;
const clergy=content.find(page=>page.slug==='our-clergy')!;
const clergyBody=clergy.html.split('<h2>')[0].replace(/<img\b[^>]*>/g,'');
const storyBody=story.html.replace(/<img\b[^>]*>/g,'');
---
<Layout title="Our parish" image="/assets/parish-exterior.webp"><PageIntro title="Our parish. Our story." label="St. Peter the Apostle" description="Meet our pastor, learn how St. Peter began, and find your place in our Fort Myers parish family."/>
  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <nav class="page-jumps" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#our-parish">Our parish</a><a href="#our-patron">Saint Peter</a><a href="#our-clergy">Father Hans</a><a href="#our-story">Our story</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>
    <section class="intro-two hub-section" id="our-parish" aria-labelledby="parish-title"><div class="prose"><h2 id="parish-title">A church to call home.</h2><p>We are a community of Orthodox Christians gathered around Jesus Christ and the faith handed down by His Apostles. St. Peter belongs to the Antiochian Orthodox Christian Archdiocese.</p><p>Our parish family comes from across Southwest Florida. We gather to worship, share a meal, and encourage one another in a life of faith.</p><a class="text-link" href="/visit/">Plan your first visit <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div><figure class="hub-photo"><img src="/assets/parish-exterior.webp" width="500" height="362" alt="The entrance to St. Peter Orthodox Church on Hickory Drive"/><figcaption>Our parish home on Hickory Drive.</figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="patron-section hub-section" id="our-patron" aria-labelledby="patron-title"><figure><img src="/assets/saint-peter-icon.webp" width="512" height="512" alt="Icon of Saint Peter the Apostle on a blue and gold background" loading="lazy"/></figure><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Our patron saint</p><h2 id="patron-title">Saint Peter the Apostle.</h2><p>Our parish bears the name of Saint Peter, an Apostle of Jesus Christ. His icon is part of our parish’s identity and a reminder of the apostolic faith at the heart of our life together.</p><p>We seek to follow Christ in prayer, worship, and love for our neighbors.</p><a class="text-link" href="/orthodoxy/">Explore our Orthodox faith <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div></section>
    <section class="intro-two hub-section" id="our-clergy" aria-labelledby="clergy-title"><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Meet our pastor</p><h2 id="clergy-title">Father Hans Jacobse.</h2><p>Father Hans has been our pastor since St. Peter began in 2008. Ordained in 1990, he has a particular ministry supporting young men through Antiochian Men and the Brotherhood of St. Paisios.</p><p>For questions about visiting, learning the faith, or parish life, you can reach him directly. Text is the fastest way to get in touch.</p><a class="button" href="sms:+12392484775">Text Father Hans <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a><details class="parish-detail"><summary>His background and the role of a parish priest</summary><div set:html={clergyBody}/></details></div><figure class="hub-photo"><img src="/assets/who.webp" width="358" height="200" alt="Father Hans Jacobse preaching at St. Peter" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Father Hans Jacobse · Parish priest</figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="intro-two hub-section" id="our-story" aria-labelledby="story-title"><figure class="hub-photo"><img src="/assets/imported/591c1e8090379ed6.webp" width="960" height="640" alt="The Holiday Inn where St. Peter first gathered for worship" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Our first gatherings took place at a local Holiday Inn.</figcaption></figure><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Our beginnings</p><h2 id="story-title">From a little room to a parish home.</h2><p>Our first home was a room at a Holiday Inn, with everything needed for the Divine Liturgy stored in a closet. As the parish grew, we moved to a storefront in Bonita Springs and then to our home on Hickory Drive.</p><p>Our mission has remained the same: an open and loving place to worship God, where people of every background can gather and love Him and one another.</p><details class="parish-detail"><summary>Read the full parish story</summary><div set:html={storyBody}/></details></div></section>
    <section class="hub-section parish-contact" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">We would love to meet you</p><h2 id="contact-title">Stay connected.</h2><p>{site.address}<br/>{site.city}</p></div><div><a class="button" href="/contact/">Contact the parish <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a><a class="text-link" href="/news/">Read parish news <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a><a class="text-link" href="/calendar/">See the service calendar <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a></div></section>
  </div>
</Layout>
